 r←prefix RemovePackagePrefix item
⍝ Removes `prefix`, the "group-name-" part of a package ID, from `item`, so that only the version
⍝ number is left to be displayed.\\
⍝ Anything that does not start with `prefix` is returned unchanged. That matters for column [;2] of
⍝ Tatin's "later versions" report: it may carry a marker like "<<< Not available any more >>>"
⍝ rather than a package ID, and dropping a fixed number of characters off that used to leave a
⍝ fragment like "e any more >>>".
 r←item
 :If prefix≡(≢prefix)↑item
     r←(≢prefix)↓item
 :EndIf
⍝Done
